{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00834",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 12.12,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "G'day, Maureen. I'm Josie, the nurse. I'll weigh you and take your pulse before the doctor. How are you travelling? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.01,
      "end_seconds": 22.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "Oh, I'm good, love. Well, I'm tired, that's why we're here. And this is my carer, Bridget, she drives me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 40.13,
      "end_seconds": 45.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Pulse 62, blood pressure 118 over 72, weight 66 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.69,
      "end_seconds": 54.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "Hi Maureen, hi Bridget. I'm Dr Chen. So, tired. Tell me about it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.6,
      "end_seconds": 69.14,
      "duration_seconds": 12.54,
      "text": "I've been tired all the time for a month, doctor. I'm worn out by two in the afternoon. I wonder if it's my thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.13,
      "end_seconds": 75.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "Why do you wonder about the thyroid? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.2,
      "end_seconds": 87.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "Because I had it treated last year, the radioactive iodine, and I've been on the thyroid tablets since. My sister says it's the thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.82,
      "end_seconds": 96.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "That's a good thought. How are you sleeping, and how's your appetite? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.15,
      "end_seconds": 102.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "I sleep well, nine hours, and I'm eating well. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.53,
      "end_seconds": 109.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "Any feeling of being cold, constipation, dry skin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.04,
      "end_seconds": 115.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "A bit cold, yes. And dry skin on my shins."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.41,
      "end_seconds": 123.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "And your mood? Any low mood, or lost interest in things?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.25,
      "end_seconds": 132.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "No, I'm not low. I'm just tired. I'm perfectly fine in my mood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 134.78,
      "end_seconds": 145.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.07,
      "text": "She has been low, doctor. She hasn't wanted to go to her craft group for weeks. And she's cried a couple of times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 148.24,
      "end_seconds": 149.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Bridget, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.84,
      "end_seconds": 163.0,
      "duration_seconds": 12.16,
      "text": "I'll note both, Maureen, that you say your mood is fine, and Bridget's noticed you've been withdrawn. What medicines do you take?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.97,
      "end_seconds": 172.05,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "Levothyroxine, 100 micrograms, once a day, before breakfast. And vitamin D, 1000 units."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.26,
      "end_seconds": 179.59,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "Do you take the levothyroxine on an empty stomach? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.51,
      "end_seconds": 184.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Mostly. With my tea. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.54,
      "end_seconds": 189.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Tea and calcium can reduce absorption. Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.84,
      "end_seconds": 194.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "No, none, love."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.31,
      "end_seconds": 199.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.84,
      "end_seconds": 202.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "A sherry on Sundays."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.9,
      "end_seconds": 212.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "Let me look at you. Josie did your pulse, it's a little slow. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.74,
      "end_seconds": 216.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Is that bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.15,
      "end_seconds": 247.25,
      "duration_seconds": 9.1,
      "text": "It can fit with an underactive thyroid. Let me feel your thyroid area and check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.96,
      "end_seconds": 258.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "Your skin is dry, your reflexes are slow, and there's no lump in the neck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 258.81,
      "end_seconds": 262.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Is it the thyroid, doctor? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.74,
      "end_seconds": 282.01,
      "duration_seconds": 17.27,
      "text": "Possibly. After thyroid treatment, the tablet dose often needs adjusting. I'd say this could be an underactive thyroid from too low a dose, but I can't rule out another cause of tiredness, such as anaemia or low mood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.97,
      "end_seconds": 285.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "What do we do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.92,
      "end_seconds": 299.78,
      "duration_seconds": 11.86,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a blood test for your thyroid function, your blood count, and your iron and vitamin B12 levels."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 301.59,
      "end_seconds": 305.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "I can take it right now. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.49,
      "end_seconds": 314.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "And I'd like a blood sugar, to be complete."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.09,
      "end_seconds": 318.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "All right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.95,
      "end_seconds": 333.72,
      "duration_seconds": 13.77,
      "text": "In the meantime, take the levothyroxine on its own, with water, half an hour before breakfast, and don't have tea or milk with it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 336.51,
      "end_seconds": 337.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.46,
      "end_seconds": 348.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "And Maureen, if your mood gets lower, or you feel hopeless, please tell us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.55,
      "end_seconds": 352.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "I will, I promise. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.72,
      "end_seconds": 363.59,
      "duration_seconds": 9.87,
      "text": "If you get very drowsy, very cold, confused, or short of breath, come in straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.97,
      "end_seconds": 368.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
